# Goal Model for Resource Collection and Delivery Mission

## Goal Table

| Goal ID | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1      | Satisfy Resource Requests | - | Achieve | - | To ensure all requested resources are collected and delivered. |
| G2      | Collection Phase | - | Perform | AND | Must collect resources before delivery. |
| G3      | Delivery Phase | - | Perform | AND | Must deliver resources after collection. |
| G4      | Handle Low Battery During Collection | - | Perform | FALLBACK(G2, G4) | Fallback if battery drops below 10%. |
| G2.1    | Collect Resources from Single Storage | - | Perform | AND | Single storage requires sequential tasks. |
| G2.2    | Collect Resources from Multiple Storages | - | Perform | OR | Multiple storages can be handled by multiple robots in parallel. |
| G3.1    | Deliver Resources to Single Location | - | Perform | AND | Single delivery requires sequential tasks. |
| G3.2    | Deliver Resources to Multiple Locations | - | Perform | OR | Multiple locations can be handled by multiple robots in parallel. |

## Task Table

| Task ID | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Move to Storage Location | AND | Storage Location | 1 | Single robot per storage. |
| AT2     | Request Resources from Storage | AND | Storage Location | 1 | Single robot per storage. |
| AT3     | Move to Delivery Location | AND | Delivery Location | 1 | Single delivery point. |
| AT4     | Deliver Resources | AND | Delivery Location | 1 | Single delivery point. |
| AT5     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | FALLBACK | Recharging Station | 1 | Ensure mission continuity. |
| AT6     | Return Resource to Checkpoint | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Single robot per resource. |
| AT7     | Trigger Alert for Failed Return | AND | Central Control | 1 | Single action for alerting. |
| AT8     | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Ensure mission continuity. |

## Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both collection and delivery are necessary for the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either single or multiple storages can be handled.

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**  
  Justification: Sequential tasks for single storage.

- **G2.2 -> AT1, AT2 (Parallel)**  
  Justification: Multiple robots can collect from different storages simultaneously.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either single or multiple deliveries can be handled.

- **G3.1 -> AT3, AT4 [AND]**  
  Justification: Sequential tasks for single delivery.

- **G4 -> AT5, AT6, AT7, AT8 [AND]**  
  Justification: Sequential fallback actions for low battery.

This goal model ensures efficient resource management with parallel and sequential task execution, handling both normal and contingency scenarios.
